# Pin execution-evidence artifacts to LF line endings on checkout.
#
# Without this file, a checkout with Git's own Windows-recommended default
# (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites LF blobs to CRLF in the working tree. The
# SHA256 values recorded in each scenario's experiment_manifest.json were
# computed against the LF-committed content, so a CRLF working-tree copy
# fails that hash check on any such checkout — not because the content
# changed, but because the line endings did. This does not retroactively
# fix already-generated manifests; it prevents the same failure for future
# runs and for anyone re-verifying existing evidence going forward.
results/execution_evidence/** text eol=lf
